      "id": "sol.amc-10a-2020-p8.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Group the terms in blocks of four: \\((1+2+3-4)\\) \\(+(5+6+7-8)\\) \\(+\\cdots\\) \\(+(197+198+199-200)\\). The \\(j\\)th block is \\((4j-3)+(4j-2)\\) \\(+(4j-1)-4j=8j-6\\).\n\nThere are \\(50\\) blocks, so the sum is \\(\\sum_{j=1}^{50}(8j-6)=8\\cdot\\dfrac{50\\cdot51}{2}\\) \\(-6\\cdot50=9900\\). Thus, B is the correct answer.",
      "hints": [
        "Group the expression into blocks of four terms",
        "Find a formula for the \\(j\\)th block and sum over \\(50\\) blocks"
      ],
